                                "sense_id": "dfd2ad57-350b-39da-ba5c-a61e2f100c4f",
                                "text": "The parent had put pins by papersful, / Till she was like a frightful porcupine;[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66c643ef-a19f-4fbd-bb43-525b6823388e",
                                "sense_id": "dfd2ad57-350b-39da-ba5c-a61e2f100c4f",
                                "text": "At various drugstores in such places as Purdy’s, Golden’s Bridge, Brewster, Croton Falls, Katonah and Mount Kisco, as well as Ridgefield, Scotts Corners, Pound Ridge and New Caanan, I bought about a ton of eye makeup, lipstick, powder, papersful of bobby pins, curlers (me! curlers!) and other tools for the conversion of Woman As Harper’s Bazaar Believes Her To Be."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "abfd9312-0f88-45f0-81b2-8da336c95067",
                                "sense_id": "dfd2ad57-350b-39da-ba5c-a61e2f100c4f",
                                "text": "Yvonne scooped up two more paperfuls of flour by the time he returned with her broom and dustpan."
